BlastEm Fedora snapshot source
==============================

The RPM source archive is generated from this exact commit on upstream master:

    2dd605c6e27971f67ce5b8363cc858964f99aa50

The rpm-builder profile uses its git_archive strategy, with this archive name
and top-level prefix:

    blastem-2dd605c6e27971f67ce5b8363cc858964f99aa50.tar.gz
    blastem-2dd605c6e27971f67ce5b8363cc858964f99aa50/

Equivalent source content can be produced from a clean clone with:

    git archive --format=tar.gz \
        --prefix=blastem-2dd605c6e27971f67ce5b8363cc858964f99aa50/ \
        --output=blastem-2dd605c6e27971f67ce5b8363cc858964f99aa50.tar.gz \
        2dd605c6e27971f67ce5b8363cc858964f99aa50

No moving branch name is used as source input. Packaging files are staged from
the fedora/44 branch separately and are not included in the upstream archive.

The archive produced twice with Git 2.51.0 during packaging validation was
byte-for-byte identical and had this SHA-256 digest:

    b80b80aee99c9189205ffc65231bf4e8ba29b8d1ab7c38bd46ce916c40b7aca6

The digest records the validated archive. Git's archive and compression
implementations are part of the source-generation environment, so the pinned
commit and prefix above remain the authoritative content identity.
